<h2>Requirement description</h2>

<p>
This requirement is concerned with ensuring that technology selections are made deliberately and with appropriate reference to NHS England strategic direction, the NHS England Technology Radar, and relevant industry developments.
</p>

<p>
Technology choices should not be based solely on individual preference, supplier recommendation or familiarity. Decisions should be informed by recognised governance processes, technology strategy, architectural objectives and evidence-based evaluation.
</p>

<p>
The objective is to improve consistency, reduce unnecessary technology proliferation, and encourage adoption of technologies that are supportable, sustainable and aligned with organisational goals.
</p>

<p>
<strong>In simple terms:</strong><br>
Technology decisions should be aligned to NHS England strategy and informed by both the Technology Radar and wider market knowledge.
</p>

