<h2>What assessors should look for</h2>

<ol>
<li>
<strong>Strategic alignment</strong> – Are technology decisions aligned with NHS England direction and objectives?
</li>

<li>
<strong>Technology Radar consideration</strong> – Has the NHS England Technology Radar been considered as part of the decision process?
</li>

<li>
<strong>Options evaluation</strong> – Have realistic technology alternatives been assessed before selection?
</li>

<li>
<strong>Industry awareness</strong> – Is there evidence that wider industry practices and market developments have been considered?
</li>

<li>
<strong>Decision governance</strong> – Have technology selections been reviewed through appropriate architecture and governance processes?
</li>

<li>
<strong>Documented rationale</strong> – Can the team explain why the chosen technology was selected over other options?
</li>
</ol>

<h2>What separates a 3 from a 4 or 5</h2>

<p>
A score of <strong>3</strong> generally means there is evidence that technology decisions have been considered and justified, but the assessment may not be comprehensive, consistently documented or clearly aligned with strategic guidance.
</p>

<p>
A score of <strong>4</strong> requires evidence that technology choices are routinely assessed against organisational direction, Technology Radar recommendations and alternative options. Governance and architecture review activities should support the decisions.
</p>

<p>
A score of <strong>5</strong> requires technology selection to be embedded within a mature decision-making process. Evidence should demonstrate proactive evaluation of emerging technologies, strong strategic alignment, well-documented trade-offs and governance-supported decision-making that influences future architecture direction.
</p>

<h2>Suggested evidence examples (not SAF-mandated artefacts)</h2>

<ul>
<li>Technology options assessments</li>
<li>Architecture Decision Records (ADRs)</li>
<li>Technology Radar review outputs</li>
<li>Solution Design Overview documents</li>
<li>Architecture governance papers</li>
<li>Technology standards assessments</li>
<li>Market or supplier evaluations</li>
<li>Technical strategy documents</li>
<li>Design Authority review records</li>
<li>Technology roadmap documentation</li>
</ul>



